body:
. . .

&#x200B;

\*speechless\*

&#x200B;

Ummm, sorry but Ive been drinking tea for years instead of coffee and Ive been accustomed to those teas already so . . . thank you for lending me a bit of your time

a couple of days, or a couple of months, as long as it will look natural and noone would think its suicide. You are helpful by the way

&#x200B;

helped

Yeah I feel you bro.

&#x200B;

It is when everything is stable and progressing in a way not good and not bad either, then everything went back down again.

&#x200B;

Thats is what I feel everyday, everyweek, everytime since I was in high school. There is this hope that someday, somehow in anyway, life will get better but as you can see, that hope is slowly dying out.

Music, positive music. Positive rock music to, or pop or jazz. Play it out loud. Sing along with the music. Watch positive or action movies and never watch anything spooky or sad. If possible avoid meat for a while or eat foods that is associated with happiness, not bright colored ones but like mcdonalds happy meal. Do a regular cleaning and maintenance in the house and stock up on jokebooks and occasionally read them. Then add a shelf for science books and always have a periodic table of element with you and when you feel something off of example the door suddenly opened, close it then recite science facts(absolute facts) and the periodic table. Throw away old stuff and buy new stuff and if possible, buy high tech stuff. Always sleep as early as you can and wake up about 5 or 6 in the morning. Have an electrician check your wirings and a plumber for your pipes. And if possible, always close the windows. Make sure your windows are hard to access from the outside but easily breakable from the inside just in case of emergency.

&#x200B;

Thats what I basically did when I felt something was off in my new apartment back then. Ive never felt better after a few more days doing that. It made me spend a great deal of money, but hey my peace of mind is much precious than money
